        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Puori PW1 is one of the few protein powders where the clean-label pitch is backed by something you can check: batch results tied to the bag in your hand. The label is short, the sweetener is coconut sugar rather than sucralose, and the whey comes from grass-fed herds. For buyers who want exactly that, it is a sound choice, and Bourbon Vanilla or Unflavored are the versions to start with.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For everyone else, the smaller scoop and premium price are hard to ignore. Tested athletes should choose an NSF or Informed Sport product, lactose-sensitive buyers an isolate, and budget-first buyers a mainstream whey. Our <a href="/best-clean-protein-powder/">best clean protein powder guide</a> lays out all of those options side by side.
